@page "/events"

<PageTitle>Events · Bortable</PageTitle>

<div class="bb-intro">
    <h1>Events</h1>
    <p class="bb-subtitle">
        Every drag fires the SortableJS-style lifecycle callbacks - <code>OnStart</code>, <code>OnChange</code>,
        <code>OnUpdate</code>, <code>OnRemove</code>, <code>OnAdd</code>, <code>OnSort</code> and <code>OnEnd</code>.
        Drag items within and between the lists and watch the log - the newest event is on top.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="bb-demo">
    <EventLog />
</div>

<DemoCode For="typeof(EventLog)" />

<section class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-primary"></span> Try it</h3>
    <ul class="bb-detail-list">
        <li>Drag <em>Item 1</em> below <em>Item 3</em>: <code>OnStart</code>, then on the drop <code>OnUpdate</code>, <code>OnSort</code> and <code>OnEnd</code>.</li>
        <li>
            Drag <em>Item 4</em> into the right list: <code>OnRemove</code> on the left, <code>OnAdd</code> on the right,
            <code>OnSort</code> on both, and <code>OnEnd</code> on the left - the list the drag started in.
        </li>
        <li>Drag an item into the other list and back home before you drop it: nothing changed, so only <code>OnStart</code> and <code>OnEnd</code>.</li>
        <li>Tick the box and drag again: an <code>OnChange</code> line for every place the item passes through.</li>
        <li>
            Pick an item up from the keyboard (<kbd>Space</kbd>), move it, and press <kbd>Escape</kbd>: <code>OnEnd</code>
            alone, with <code>keyboard</code> and <code>canceled</code> in its flags.
        </li>
    </ul>
</section>

<section class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-success"></span> The lifecycle</h3>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Event</th><th>Raised when</th><th>On</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnStart</code></td><td>A drag begins.</td><td>The source list.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnChange</code></td><td>The dragged item takes a new position during the drag.</td><td>The list it moves in.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnUpdate</code></td><td>The order of the list changed within the same list.</td><td>The list.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnRemove</code></td><td>An item was moved out to another list (not raised for a clone).</td><td>The source list.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnAdd</code></td><td>An item was dropped in from another list.</td><td>The destination list.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnSort</code></td><td>Any change to a list: add, remove or update.</td><td>Each list that changed.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OnEnd</code></td><td>The drag ended, whatever its outcome.</td><td>The source list.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">
        The completion events are raised after the bound lists have changed and <code>ItemsChanged</code> has been
        raised, so a handler sees the final state. Within a list: <code>OnUpdate</code>, <code>OnSort</code>,
        <code>OnEnd</code>. Across lists: <code>OnRemove</code> on the source (unless it is a clone), <code>OnAdd</code>
        on the destination, <code>OnSort</code> on the source (unless it is a clone) and on the destination, then
        <code>OnEnd</code>. A cancelled drag raises <code>OnEnd</code> alone. All of them are raised once the drag is
        over, so a handler that takes its time - a save to a server, say - never holds up the next drag.
    </p>
</section>

<section class="bb-card">
    <h3 class="bb-card-title"><span class="bb-dot bb-dot-warning"></span> The event arguments</h3>
    <p class="bb-card-desc">Every event passes a <code>BortableEventArgs&lt;TItem&gt;</code>:</p>
    <div class="bb-scroll">
        <table class="bb-table">
            <thead>
                <tr><th>Member</th><th>What it says</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>Item</code></td><td>The dragged item - the copy, in the events after a clone was dropped.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>Items</code></td><td>Every item the drag moved: a <a href="multi-drag">multi-drag</a> selection, or just <code>Item</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>OldIndex</code>, <code>NewIndex</code></td><td>Where the item was in the source list when the drag started, and where it is in the destination.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>FromId</code>, <code>ToId</code></td><td>The <code>Id</code> of the source and of the destination list.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>FromGroup</code>, <code>ToGroup</code></td><td>Their <code>Group</code>.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>CrossedLists</code></td><td><code>true</code> when the item moved between lists.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>Input</code></td><td>How the drag was made: <code>Mouse</code>, <code>Touch</code>, <code>Pen</code>, <code>Keyboard</code>, or <code>Api</code> for a move made by code.</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>IsClone</code></td><td><code>true</code> when a copy goes into another list and the original stays (see <a href="cloning">cloning</a>).</td></tr>
                <tr><td class="bb-table-key"><code>Canceled</code></td><td>On <code>OnEnd</code>: the drag kept nothing - cancelled, spilled with <code>RevertOnSpill</code>, refused by <code>ConfirmDrop</code> or, for a multi-drag's gathering, by <code>CanDrop</code> (see <a href="rules">rules</a>), or ended as its list left the page with a <code>ConfirmDrop</code> to ask.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</section>
